messages:
Marta (Docs): heads-up i'm preparing a tiny docs PR clarifying tiered quotas: header names, downgrade behavior, small SDK snippets, and one grafana/promql example. will open shortly.

Alex (DevEx): great — please keep snippets <=6 lines so quickstart can use them. include fallback for legacy headers.

Marta (Docs): draft node snippet: ```js
const r = await fetch(url, { headers });
const rem = r.headers.get('X-Redwood-Quota-Remaining') || r.headers.get('X-Quota-Remaining');
console.log('remaining:', Number(rem || 0));
```

Ben (Eng): prod headers are X-Redwood-Quota-*; legacy X-Quota-* still works. tiny express middleware to attach quota info: app.use((req,res,next)=>{const r=res.getHeader('X-Redwood-Quota-Remaining')||res.getHeader('X-Quota-Remaining');req.quota={remaining:Number(r||0)};next()})

Sumi (Billing): on downgrades please say: "typically a short (~7 day) grace period; enterprise agreements may differ" and link billing playbook. add quick reconciliation tip: use billing exports + redwood_tokens_consumed_total for spot checks.

Marta (Docs): added cautious downgrade language and the reconciliation note. grafana promql (7d, exclude tests): sum by(customer_tier)(increase(redwood_tokens_consumed_total{env="prod",customer_type!~"internal|test"}[7d])) Legend: {{customer_tier}}

DocsBot: Reminder: include changelog entry, migration note, and billing-playbook crosslink in PR template.

Marta (Docs): thanks all — opening PR at 1788890500 and will tag @Alex, @Ben, @Sumi for review. small doc fixes like this really help support. :tada:
